  "id": "COMPOUND:32178 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Cryptobeilic Acid B is implicated in the interaction with the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit through a series of molecular pathways involving taste receptor type 2 member 31. This receptor, which is targeted by multiple compounds, appears to be a key mediator in the interaction between Cryptobeilic Acid B and the hemagglutinin subunit. The evidence suggests that Cryptobeilic Acid B acts as a target for several compounds, including (3R,4S,6S)-10,13-dihydroxy-3-methoxy-6-methyl-5-oxapentacyclo[9.7.0.02,8.04,6.012,17]octadeca-1,8,10,12(17),13,15-hexaene-7,18-dione, (2s,4r)-4-Hydroxy-4-methyl-glutamic acid, and 8,19-Dihydroxyserrulat-14-Ene. These compounds are all known to target the same receptor, which in turn is linked to the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Cryptobeilic Acid B may modulate the activity of the taste receptor, which then influences the hemagglutinin subunit. The evidence supports a role for the taste receptor in the interaction between Cryptobeilic Acid B and the hemagglutinin subunit, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
